<!-- CAREER -->

<section class="pathway-section" id="career">

<div class="pathway-header">

<div class="pathway-number">03</div>

<div>

<h2>
Career Advancement Intelligence
</h2>

<p>
Your current job may contain more career capital than you realize.
The goal is to identify the systems, responsibilities,
metrics, and problems hidden inside the work you already perform.
</p>

</div>

</div>


<div class="lesson">

<div class="lesson-label">
Career Translation Principle
</div>

<h3>
Do not describe only what you did.
Translate what the work proves.
</h3>

<p>
"I worked inventory" is a task description.
"I maintained inventory accuracy and identified discrepancies"
is a capability description.
"I reduced recurring inventory errors by identifying the source"
becomes an impact statement.
</p>

</div>


<div class="resource-cards">

<div class="resource-card">
<h4>📈 Achievement Ledger</h4>
<p>
Record problems solved, improvements made,
customer issues resolved, and responsibilities expanded.
</p>
</div>

<div class="resource-card">
<h4>🔄 Transferable Skills</h4>
<p>
Translate customer service, scheduling, inventory,
operations, sales, and administration into business capabilities.
</p>
</div>

<div class="resource-card">
<h4>📋 Internal Job Intelligence</h4>
<p>
Internal openings reveal which skills the organization values.
Use them as a roadmap.
</p>
</div>

<div class="resource-card">
<h4>🧩 System Problems</h4>
<p>
Recurring operational problems can become opportunities
to demonstrate analytical thinking and initiative.
</p>
</div>

<div class="resource-card">
<h4>🗣 Better Feedback</h4>
<p>
Instead of asking "How am I doing?"
ask which behaviors would make you more valuable for the next level.
</p>
</div>

<div class="resource-card">
<h4>📊 Promotion Evidence File</h4>
<p>
Maintain documentation of accomplishments throughout the year.
</p>
</div>

</div>


<br>


<div class="decision">

<div class="decision-card">

<strong>
Low visibility?
</strong>

Create measurable documentation
of your contributions.

</div>

<div class="decision-card">

<strong>
Low credentials?
</strong>

Build projects or certifications
aligned with target roles.

</div>

<div class="decision-card">

<strong>
Low experience?
</strong>

Use current responsibilities to
generate transferable evidence.

</div>

</div>

</section>


<!-- BUSINESS -->

<section class="pathway-section" id="business">

<div class="pathway-header">

<div class="pathway-number">04</div>

<div>

<h2>
Entrepreneurship Intelligence
</h2>

<p>
Entrepreneurship does not begin with a logo, website,
business card, or large inventory order.
It begins with evidence that someone has a problem worth solving.
</p>

</div>

</div>


<div class="lesson">

<div class="lesson-label">
Capital-Light Principle
</div>

<h3>
Use customer information as a form of capital.
</h3>

<p>
Before spending money, learn.
Interview potential customers.
Study complaints.
Analyze competitors.
Identify repeated tasks.
Find expensive inefficiencies.
Test a small service.
</p>

<br>

<p>
The objective is to reduce uncertainty before increasing spending.
</p>

</div>


<div class="resource-cards">

<div class="resource-card">
<h4>🔍 Complaint Mining</h4>
<p>
Study reviews, forums, support questions,
and public discussions to identify recurring problems.
</p>
</div>

<div class="resource-card">
<h4>🧪 Service Before Product</h4>
<p>
A service can test demand before investing in software,
inventory, manufacturing, or complicated products.
</p>
</div>

<div class="resource-card">
<h4>📞 Customer Interviews</h4>
<p>
Ask how potential customers currently solve the problem,
what it costs, and what makes existing solutions frustrating.
</p>
</div>

<div class="resource-card">
<h4>🧱 Manual First</h4>
<p>
Perform a process manually before building technology around it.
</p>
</div>

<div class="resource-card">
<h4>🤝 Partnership Leverage</h4>
<p>
Look for organizations that already have the audience you need.
</p>
</div>

<div class="resource-card">
<h4>💰 Pre-Sale Testing</h4>
<p>
Where appropriate, validate whether people will commit before
building the full offer.
</p>
</div>

</div>


<br>


<div class="experiment">

<div class="experiment-card">
<small>EXPERIMENT 01</small>
<h4>Problem Interview</h4>
<p>
Talk to potential users and identify repeated pain points.
</p>
</div>

<div class="experiment-card">
<small>EXPERIMENT 02</small>
<h4>Manual Service</h4>
<p>
Deliver the outcome manually before building a system.
</p>
</div>

<div class="experiment-card">
<small>EXPERIMENT 03</small>
<h4>Small Offer</h4>
<p>
Create a narrow offer around one specific problem.
</p>
</div>

<div class="experiment-card">
<small>EXPERIMENT 04</small>
<h4>Distribution Test</h4>
<p>
Test whether you can reach potential customers consistently.
</p>
</div>

</div>

</section>


